<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="a00d1df7">&lt;h5&gt;
    Weigh the cost of each strategy against the level of risk
&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    All projects have risk. Strategies to manage risk come at a cost. For example, adding formal user reviews to manage the
    risk of user acceptance adds time and cost to the project. Carefully weigh the consequences of each project risk
    against the cost of strategies used to manage it.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;
    Examine interdependencies of risks
&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    When developing a strategy to manage risk, examine the relationships and dependencies among risks. A strategy to reduce
    risk in one area can increase risk in another. For example, a decision to reduce the risk of a lengthy project by
    increasing team size will increase the risk of ineffective team coordination and communication.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
