<attribute name="sectionName" nodeId="5c0eed03"></attribute>
<attribute name="sectionDescription" nodeId="5fec43f9">&lt;p&gt;
    For each project risk, identify contingent actions that could be taken if a risk occurred.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Contingent actions are reactive and are invoked only if a risk actually occurs. For example,&lt;br /&gt;
    if one of the project risks is that the hardware may not be installed in time for the planned&lt;br /&gt;
    pilot site, identify contingent actions, such as an alternative pilot site. The process of&lt;br /&gt;
    identifying contingent actions can require modifications to the project workplan to allow&lt;br /&gt;
    more flexibility for these types of situations.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Document the contingent actions and adjust the plans as necessary.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
